tuple typing, so I'll follow that same structure for the capsule options.\n\nNow I'm computing the font colors array from primary, secondary, and optional background symbol colors, then using it in the grid item to render each symbol display with the selected state and rendering strategy.\n\nI'm updating the colors prop on the child to accept an array instead of a single value, and keeping the rendering strategy default. I want to verify the @Prop updates actually propagate through LazyForEach before moving on to the color picker builder.\n\nI'm also realizing the @Builder function for the color picker passes its current-color parameter by value, which in ArkTS V1 means state changes won't trigger UI refresh inside the builder — I need to either read `this.xxx` directly inside the builder or wrap it in a component instead.\n\nI'm weighing whether to avoid builder parameters entirely by writing a builder that reads state directly from `this` within the parent's render context, so updates stay tracked.\n\nWriting the color group builder...\n\nI real","startTime":1792412740738,"lastModifiedTime":1792412763488},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_014knrzyb7nqdzLAQdSFrHra","type":"TOOL","toolName":"read_file","params":{"file_path":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/sym-combo-customize/entry/src/main/ets/pages/Index.ets","offset":"95","limit":"25"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"<file>\n    95→}\n    96→\n    97→@Component\n    98→struct LinysSymbolDisplay {\n    99→  @Prop symbol: linysSymbol;\n   100→  @Link selected: linysSymbol;\n   101→  // Colors\n   102→  @Prop colors: ResourceColor = $r('app.color.font_color_title');\n   103→  @Prop fontWeight: FontWeight = FontWeight.Normal;\n   104→\n   105→  build() {\n   106→    Column({ space: 10 }) {\n   107→      SymbolGlyph($r('sys.symbol.'.concat(this.symbol.name)))\n   108→        .fontColor([$r('app.color.font_color_title')])\n   109→        .width(50)\n   110→        .height(50)\n   111→        .fontWeight(this.fon